Dark Kitchen's workflow engine removes provider-specific SDK coupling and adds
semantic role routing, deterministic nested/parallel call identities, durable
journal replay, bounded concurrency/retries, and structured cancellation.

The upstream copyright and complete MIT license text are retained in
packages/workflow-engine/NOTICE.md. Third-party packages distributed through
npm or the container retain their own licenses and notices in their package
metadata/files. Optional managed capability providers download separately
pinned upstream artifacts only after an explicit provisioning plan and
approval; their upstream licenses apply to those artifacts.
